c</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Linhartova</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Havlicek</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Sebo</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A novel "clip-and-link" activity of repeat in toxin (RTX) proteins from gram-negative pathogens. Covalent protein cross-linking by an Asp-Lys isopeptide bond upon calcium-dependent processing at an Asp-Pro bond</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2004</year><volume>279</volume><fpage>24944</fpage><lpage>24956</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15044436</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.M314013200</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kamp</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Popma</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Anakotta</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Smits</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of hemolytic and cytotoxic proteins of <italic>Actinobacillus pleuropneumoniae </italic>by use of monoclonal antibodies</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>1991</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>3079</fpage><lpage>3085</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1879932</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kamp</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Stockhofe-Zurwieden</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>van Leengoed</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Smits</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Endobronchial inoculation with Apx toxins of <italic>Actinobacillus pleuropneumoniae </italic>leads to pleuropneumonia in pigs</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year